    "chunk_id": "journal-003_chunk_0",
    "document_id": "journal-003",
    "content": "I reviewed the architecture of a web application I have been working with and tried to understand it as a set of responsibilities rather than a collection of folders. The frontend handles presentation and interaction, the API coordinates business operations, repositories manage persistence, and background workers handle tasks that do not need to block a request.",
    "metadata": {
      "date": "2026-01-10",
      "topic": "Software Architecture",
      "entry_id": "journal-003",
      "source": "C:\\Users\\Home\\Documents\\ragJournal\\dataset\\03_2026-01-10_software_architecture.md",
      "filename": "03_2026-01-10_software_architecture.md",
      "file_type": "markdown",
      "title": "Software Architecture",
      "date_object": "2026-01-10",
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "chunking_method": "semantic",
      "sentence_start": 0,
      "sentence_end": 1,
      "sentence_count": 2
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "journal-003_chunk_1",
    "document_id": "journal-003",
    "content": "Thinking this way made several design decisions easier to explain. I also noticed areas where boundaries are not clean and a change in one layer often requires changes elsewhere.",
    "metadata": {
      "date": "2026-01-10",
      "topic": "Software Architecture",
      "entry_id": "journal-003",
      "source": "C:\\Users\\Home\\Documents\\ragJournal\\dataset\\03_2026-01-10_software_architecture.md",
      "filename": "03_2026-01-10_software_architecture.md",
      "file_type": "markdown",
      "title": "Software Architecture",
      "date_object": "2026-01-10",
      "chunk_index": 1,
      "chunking_method": "semantic",
      "sentence_start": 2,
      "sentence_end": 3,
      "sentence_count": 2
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "journal-003_chunk_2",
    "document_id": "journal-003",
    "content": "I wrote down examples of coupling so I can discuss them later when studying refactoring. One important lesson is that architecture is not about creating as many layers as possible.",
    "metadata": {
      "date": "2026-01-10",
      "topic": "Software Architecture",
      "entry_id": "journal-003",
      "source": "C:\\Users\\Home\\Documents\\ragJournal\\dataset\\03_2026-01-10_software_architecture.md",
      "filename": "03_2026-01-10_software_architecture.md",
      "file_type": "markdown",
      "title": "Software Architecture",
      "date_object": "2026-01-10",
      "chunk_index": 2,
      "chunking_method": "semantic",
      "sentence_start": 4,
      "sentence_end": 5,
      "sentence_count": 2
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "journal-003_chunk_3",
    "document_id": "journal-003",
    "content": "Every abstraction should have a reason, and the cost of indirection should be justified by the problem it solves.",
    "metadata": {
      "date": "2026-01-10",
      "topic": "Software Architecture",
      "entry_id": "journal-003",
      "source": "C:\\Users\\Home\\Documents\\ragJournal\\dataset\\03_2026-01-10_software_architecture.md",
      "filename": "03_2026-01-10_software_architecture.md",
      "file_type": "markdown",
      "title": "Software Architecture",
      "date_object": "2026-01-10",
      "chunk_index": 3,
      "chunking_method": "semantic",
      "sentence_start": 6,
      "sentence_end": 6,
